---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Tien Nguyen designs and leads applied AI for enterprise. AI product manager and product owner in Ho Chi Minh City."
>
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Applied AI for enterprise</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I design and lead an enterprise AI platform that turns complex workflows into governed
      operations. I connect product strategy, system design, and delivery as AI product manager and
      product owner.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">How I run it</p>
      <h2>One operating loop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Observe → Detect → Explain → Recommend → Approve → Execute → Verify → Learn. Knowledge,
        orchestration, evaluation, and governance stay on that chain instead of sitting in separate
        tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        Day to day: RAG, ReAct agents, multi-agent orchestration, human-in-the-loop workflows,
        persistent memory, runtime controls, and evidence-based verification.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
      <h2>Green SM / GSM (Vingroup), platform ops</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Day job: platform operations across Green SM ecosystems under Vingroup (
        <a href="https://www.greensm.com/vn-vi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >greensm.com</a
        >). Title and timeline go on the resume. Internals stay confidential.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label="Career overview">
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Track record</h3>
        <p>
          Over seven years I have built and scaled B2B fintech, payments, transportation, and
          enterprise systems from 0-to-1 through high-scale operations. Colonial Surety is earlier
          insurtech delivery on the resume only.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Public proof</h3>
        <p>
          Knowledge Engine, Sport Quant, and Recon are live. Gelato is the broader platform still
          under construction: a control plane plus six verticals.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Also in flight</h3>
        <p>
          Petmood (pet triage beta, HCMC), AnDigi (insurance operated by agents, still in design),
          and advisory work with Vietnam fashion-retail SMEs.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Next</p>
      <h2>Open the live systems, then ask about employers.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Start with Knowledge Engine, then Sport Quant, then Recon. Green SM and Colonial stay on the
        resume and in conversation. They are not public product tours.
      </p>
      <div class="action-row">
        <a class="button" href={withBase('/works/')}>Case studies</a>
        <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/Tien-Nguyen-CV.pdf')}>Resume PDF</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
